    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d42">

                <pb facs="0055" n="43" xml:id="pg43"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">740.0011 European War, 1939/19015: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Ambassador in Brazil</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Caffery</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps">Rio de
                                Janeiro</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1942-01-28T20:00:00-03:00">January 28, 1942—8
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received 8:24 p.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>270. Aranha announced at the close of his closing speech (7:30 p.m.) rupture of
                    relations and also settlement of Peru and Ecuador dispute.</p>
                <p>He explained that appropriate communication was being made to Axis
                    representatives here and in Axis capitals. Delegation will send full
                    details.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Caffery</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
